  "readme": [
    {
      "section": "dsh-chrome-operation",
      "text": "A DSH plugin that turns your local Chrome browser into a set of DSH tools. It pairs with the **chrome operation** (chrome-operation) MV3 Chrome extension, which runs a WebSocket bridge inside your browser. The DSH plugin dials that bridge over loopback and exposes browser actions as DSH tools, so DSH agents can drive a real local Chrome browser."
    },
    {
      "section": "How it works",
      "text": "1. The **chrome-operation** extension (MV3) runs a background service worker that listens on\n   `ws://127.0.0.1:18765/ext/bridge` (with a 15-second keep-alive ping so the Chrome service worker doesn't go idle and drop the connection).\n2. The **dsh-chrome-operation** DSH plugin starts, connects to that WS bridge, and registers the `browser_*` tools.\n3. When DSH calls a `browser_*` tool, the request flows over the bridge and the extension performs the action in a real Chrome tab."
    },
    {
      "section": "1. Load the Chrome extension",
      "text": "1. Open `chrome://extensions`.\n2. Enable **Developer mode** (top-right).\n3. Click **Load unpacked** and select the `chrome-operation` extension directory.\n4. A token is written to `chrome.storage.local.token` (managed by the extension / `issue-token` dev script)."
    },
    {
      "section": "2. Install the DSH plugin",
      "text": "The plugin is distributed on npm as `dsh-chrome-operation`.\n\n```bash\ndsh plugin add dsh-chrome-operation\n```"
    },
    {
      "section": "3. Restart DSH",
      "text": "The plugin activates on a profile restart. Restart DSH desktop, then confirm the connection (the plugin logs `bridge ready` / `extension connected`)."
    },
    {
      "section": "Tools exposed",
      "text": "`browser_snapshot`, `browser_get_text`, `browser_navigate`, `browser_open_tab`, `browser_list_tabs`, `browser_close_tab`, `browser_click`, `browser_type`, `browser_press`, `browser_scroll`, `browser_wait`, `browser_back`, `browser_forward`, `browser_reload`."
    },
    {
      "section": "Configuration",
      "text": "- The bridge listens on loopback only (`127.0.0.1`) — local use only.\n- The extension reads the `token` from `chrome.storage.local`.\n- The default WS `pingIntervalMs` is `15000` (configurable via the bridge config endpoint `/ext/bridge-config`). Chrome's service worker goes idle ~30s; the 15s ping keeps it awake."
    },
    {
      "section": "Notes",
      "text": "- Requires **Chrome** (the extension is MV3 and uses a service worker).\n- On complex pages `browser_snapshot` may return empty; prefer `browser_get_text` + navigation for reading content.\n- If DSH ever complains about the `dshWorkshop` block, delete that top-level key — the plugin still loads via `cordis.patch.yml`."
    },
    {
      "section": "License",
      "text": "MIT"
    }
  ],
